"""Packomania's centres for the circular quadrant, N = 449..539, are not all at a local maximum of the radius, and many
have better packings close by. Local search from the published centres beat the published radius by more than 1e-12
relative for 84 of the 91 N, by up to 7.1e-05 (N = 496): sequential linear programming on the active contacts
(ccq.maximize) to convergence, 90 s per N of shaking all centres by 0.01 to 1 percent of the radius and re-
maximizing, keeping rises, then maximizing at steps from 1e-2 to 1e-10 of the radius until a whole sweep leaves the
exact radius unchanged, so a fresh ccq.maximize pass gains nothing. For the other N the published centres are kept.
These packings are the bar the task scores against. R is the exact radius of the binary64 centres as (a, b, c) for a
+ b sqrt(c) with rationals a, b, c, COORDS the centres as base64 of little-endian binary64 x y pairs, one string per
N. SCiEL run quad4491 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the exact radius for 68 N, and those packings
replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run qb4491 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the exact radius for 66 N,
and those packings replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run qc4491 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the
exact radius for 59 N, and those packings replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run qe4491 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these
packings) then raised the exact radius for 66 N, and those packings replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run qf4491
(Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the exact radius for 63 N, and those packings replace the earlier
ones. SCiEL run qg4491 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the exact radius for 67 N, and those packings
replace the earlier ones. SCiEL run qh4491 (Qwen3.8-27B, from these packings) then raised the exact radius for 70 N,
and those packings replace the earlier ones."""

